  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed dormer roof extension to main roof and roof to outrigger, owing to its excessive depth, design and siting, is considered to result in a dominant and incongruous form of development to the detriment of the existing character and appearance of the host property and terrace in which it forms part of. Therefore, the proposal fails to comply with polices D3 and D4 of the London Plan 2021, policies D12.3 and D12.4.",
    "Reason : 2 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice \r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
